  "scope": "Two parsed fixture pairs compose three case stages inside a constructor index field. One recovers a finite case returning Switch, then a Switch case returning Payload, then a Payload case swapping its distinct fields. The other recovers a Switch case returning a finite injection before the finite and Payload cases. Both resume a trailing outer constructor field. Modes 36 and 37 recheck Pick and keep, preparation, proof sealing and runtime equality with opaque twins. Direct syntax rows recover the parsed Index and compare with explicit literal fields, so field order is observable. Ten scoped mutations drop semantic variants, bypass constructor or case recovery, drop an adjacent pending case, or reverse field order. Constructor recovery and field order are controls. Every mutation requires a successful isolated build and its named failure. Identical edits share verified isolated execution with unchanged input hashes, exact recipes and source hashes, matching log hashes and the required named failure.",
